1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,155
This is Floorline.

2
00:00:02,105 --> 00:00:05,421
Floorline is a money app on near testnet.

3
00:00:05,421 --> 00:00:12,328
People can hold a token called floor, borrow against it, and check the important moves with public receipts.

4
00:00:12,328 --> 00:00:14,210
No guesswork.

5
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:16,789
Here is the simple picture.

6
00:00:16,789 --> 00:00:19,907
Floor has near backing you can inspect.

7
00:00:19,907 --> 00:00:23,710
Loans are funded by lenders, not by the treasury.

8
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:28,263
And the right to repay a loan can move to someone else as an N F T.

9
00:00:28,263 --> 00:00:30,276
Now the proof.

10
00:00:30,276 --> 00:00:34,789
When floor is redeemed, the contract creates a near payout claim.

11
00:00:34,789 --> 00:00:38,921
This finalized testnet transaction shows that withdrawal.

12
00:00:38,921 --> 00:00:44,013
When someone borrows, a lender puts up the money and the borrower locks floor.

13
00:00:44,013 --> 00:00:49,065
Here the N F T changes hands, and the new owner completes repayment.

14
00:00:49,065 --> 00:00:52,210
That right is financial, not artwork.

15
00:00:52,210 --> 00:00:58,486
If nobody repays in time, the contract settles the default and allocates collateral to the lender.

16
00:00:58,486 --> 00:01:02,868
After the demo, we permanently stopped new financial risk.

17
00:01:02,868 --> 00:01:06,907
Then we verified an existing user could still exit.

18
00:01:06,907 --> 00:01:09,328
Both receipts are public.

19
00:01:09,328 --> 00:01:12,552
Forty acceptance steps were verified.

20
00:01:12,552 --> 00:01:16,565
Judges can open the proof page and run read-only checks.

21
00:01:16,565 --> 00:01:21,631
Floorline: programmable money with verifiable rights, built on near.

